  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 119 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nStrong upper level ridging will continue into next week allowing \nfor dry conditions to persist. A short wave trough will push \ninto northern US and into the eastern Great Plains on Tuesday \nnight and into Wednesday. Any precipitation associated with this\ntrough will remain to the east, however, some cooler air and \ngusty winds will likely be observed across eastern and into \nportions of north central Nebraska. There\u2019s a potential for \ngusts up to 35 mph across much of the region Wednesday afternoon\nas the trough pivots across the region. These stronger winds \nwill be brief, diminishing by Wednesday evening. \n\nAs far as temperatures go, cooler air behind the trough will\ndrop highs into the mid 50s in north central Nebraska and into\nthe low 60s in southwest Nebraska. This colder air will continue\nto impact the region through Friday with the coldest air\nremaining generally east of US-83. Here, highs on both Thursday\nand Friday will only rise into the mid 40s to mid 50s. West of\nUS-83, highs will also drop, but only low to mid 60s which will\ncontinue through the weekend. Highs across the north central\narea will be slow to increase, gradually rising into the upper\n50s by Sunday. Overnight lows will also remain fairly mild in\nthe mid to upper 30s through the week and even rising into the\nlow 40s on Tuesday night. However, the CAA pushing into the\nregion mid-week will also drop lows across the region. North\ncentral Nebraska will see lows fall into the upper 20s with lows\nelsewhere dropping into the low to mid 30s on Wednesday,\nThursday, and Friday nights. Overnight temperatures return to\nthe mid to upper 30s by Saturday night.",
